v>
<ul><li><a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Controller_reading" title=3D=
"Controller reading">Controller reading</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Controller_detection" title=3D"C=
ontroller detection">Controller detection</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Controller_port_pinout" title=3D=
"Controller port pinout">Controller port pinout</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/Four_Score" class=3D"mw-redirect=
" title=3D"Four Score">Four Score</a> 4-player adapter</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://www.nesdev.org/wiki/SNES_controller" title=3D"SNES c=
ontroller">SNES controller</a> has backward compatible protocol with the NE=
S</li></ul>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id=3D"References">References</h2>=
</div>
<div class=3D"mw-references-wrap"><ol class=3D"references">
<li id=3D"cite_note-1"><span class=3D"mw-cite-backlink"><a href=3D"https://=
www.nesdev.org/wiki/Standard_controller#cite_ref-1" aria-label=3D"Jump up" =
title=3D"Jump up">=E2=86=91</a></span> <span class=3D"reference-text"><a re=
l=3D"nofollow" class=3D"external text" href=3D"https://www.famicomworld.com=
/forum/index.php?topic=3D6701.msg167005#msg167005">Famicom World forum post=
</a>: Famicom games that do not work with pads connected through the expans=
ion port.</span>
</li>
<li id=3D"cite_note-2"><span class=3D"mw-cite-backlink"><a href=3D"https://=
